{"builder":"Build a new tool, jsonl-lint, as the repository's first npm workspace, and open one pull request for issue https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102.\n\nContext: `packages/` does not exist yet. The root `package.json` has `workspaces: [\"packages/*\"]` and a `test` script that runs `npm test --workspaces --if-present`. CI (`.github/workflows/test.yml`) runs `npm ci` then `npm test` on Node 22. Tools are plain ES modules, Node 22+, with no build step and no runtime dependencies (see CLAUDE.md).\n\nSteps:\n1. Create `packages/jsonl-lint/package.json` with `\"name\": \"jsonl-lint\"`, `\"type\": \"module\"`, `\"scripts\": { \"test\": \"node --test\" }`, a `bin` entry `{ \"jsonl-lint\": \"bin/jsonl-lint.js\" }`, `\"engines\": { \"node\": \">=22\" }`, and no `dependencies` (also no devDependencies needed). Make sure `node --test` run from the workspace finds your test files (put them under `packages/jsonl-lint/test/` with names ending in `.test.js`).\n2. Create `packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js` exporting `lint(text)` (named export). It splits text on `\\n` (strip a trailing `\\r` from each row), numbers rows from 1, skips rows that are empty or whitespace-only (they still count toward line numbers), and runs `JSON.parse` on every other row, including a final row with no trailing newline. It returns an array of `{ line, error }`, one object per row that fails, where `error` is the parse error message string. A trailing newline at the end of the file must not create a reported row. Valid input returns `[]`.\n3. Create `packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js` (starts with `#!/usr/bin/env node`, set executable). It takes one file path argument. With no argument: print a usage message to stderr and exit 2. If the file cannot be read (missing, etc.): print an error to stderr and exit 2. Otherwise run `lint` on the contents and print one line `<file>:<line>: <error>` to stdout for every error, where `<file>` is the argument as given; exit 1 if there were any errors, 0 if none. Use `process.exitCode` or `process.exit` after output is written.\n4. Write `node:test` tests in `packages/jsonl-lint/test/`: covering `lint` and the CLI (spawn `process.execPath` with the bin path using `node:child_process` `spawnSync`, on temp files under `os.tmpdir()`). Include at least: a clean file (no output, exit 0); a bad middle row (reports the right 1-based line, exit 1); a torn/unterminated last row with no trailing newline (reported, exit 1); blank lines skipped while keeping line numbers right; a missing file (stderr, exit 2); no argument (stderr, exit 2).\n5. Create `packages/jsonl-lint/README.md` describing usage, output format, exit codes (0/1/2) and the `lint(text)` API.\n6. Update the root `README.md`: replace the \"No tools yet\" bullet under \"What is here\" with a bullet listing `packages/jsonl-lint` and what it does.\n7. Run `npm install` at the repo root so `package-lock.json` includes the new workspace (otherwise `npm ci` in CI fails), and commit the updated lock file. Then run `npm ci && npm test` at the root and confirm it passes, and also try the CLI by hand on a clean file, a broken file, a missing file and no argument.\n8. Open one pull request on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test whose body contains the line `Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102`. Wait for the `test` workflow to finish at the PR head and make sure it is green; if it fails, fix it and push again to the same PR.","verifier":"Check out the pull request's head. Run `npm ci` at the repository root first. Use a scratch directory outside the repo (e.g. `mktemp -d`) for test files. One check per expect line, in order.\n\nCheck 1 — expect: \"packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <file> prints <file>:<line>: <error> for every row that is not valid JSON (1-based lines, blank lines skipped, an unterminated last line checked) and exits 1 if any, 0 if none\"\nRun: create `clean.jsonl` with `printf '{\"a\":1}\\n[2]\\n\\n\"x\"\\n'`; create `bad.jsonl` with `printf '{\"a\":1}\\n\\n{bad\\n{\"b\":2}\\n{\"torn\":'` (no trailing newline). Run `node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <scratch>/clean.jsonl; echo $?` and the same for `bad.jsonl`, passing the file path as an argument.\nPASS: clean.jsonl prints no error lines and exits 0; bad.jsonl prints a line beginning `<file>:3: ` followed by an error text and a line beginning `<file>:5: ` followed by an error text (where `<file>` is the path as passed), prints no error line for lines 1, 2 or 4, and exits 1.\nFAIL: the bin file is missing or crashes; clean exits non-zero or reports a row; bad does not report line 3 or line 5 in the `<file>:<line>: <error>` form, reports a blank or valid line, uses wrong (e.g. 0-based) line numbers, or exits other than 1.\n\nCheck 2 — expect: \"A missing file or no argument prints to stderr and exits 2\"\nRun: `node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <scratch>/does-not-exist.jsonl` and `node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js` with no argument, capturing stdout, stderr and exit status separately.\nPASS: in both cases stderr is non-empty and the exit status is 2.\nFAIL: either case exits with any status other than 2, or writes nothing to stderr.\n\nCheck 3 — expect: \"packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js exports lint(text) returning [{ line, error }]\"\nRun from the repo root: `node --input-type=module -e \"import { lint } from './packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js'; console.log(JSON.stringify(lint('{\\\"a\\\":1}\\n{bad\\n')), JSON.stringify(lint('{}\\n')))\"`. (If `lint` is only a default export, also try `import m from ...` and use `m.lint ?? m`.)\nPASS: `lint` is exported and callable; the first call returns an array containing an object with `line` equal to 2 and an `error` property holding the error; the second returns an empty array.\nFAIL: the file is missing, no `lint` export, it throws, or it returns something other than an array of `{ line, error }` objects.\n\nCheck 4 — expect: \"The workspace has its own package.json (jsonl-lint, type module, test script node --test), no runtime dependencies, and node:test tests for a clean file, a bad middle row, a torn last row, blank lines and the exit codes\"\nRun: read `packages/jsonl-lint/package.json`; run `npm test -w jsonl-lint` (or `cd packages/jsonl-lint && npm test`); read the test files.\nPASS: package.json has name `jsonl-lint`, `type` `module`, a `test` script that is `node --test` (optionally with arguments such as a test path), and no `dependencies` entries (absent or empty); the tests import from `node:test`, pass when run, and between them cover a clean file, a bad middle row, a torn (unterminated) last row, blank lines, and the exit codes.\nFAIL: any of those fields is wrong or missing, there are runtime dependencies, the tests fail or do not use `node:test`, or any of the five named cases has no test.\n\nCheck 5 — expect: \"packages/jsonl-lint/README.md exists and the root README lists the tool\"\nRun: `test -f packages/jsonl-lint/README.md` and read root `README.md`.\nPASS: the workspace README exists and the root README names the jsonl-lint tool in its list of tools.\nFAIL: the workspace README is missing, or the root README does not mention jsonl-lint.\n\nCheck 6 — expect: \"The change is one PR on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test whose body says Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102, and npm test and the test workflow are green at its head\"\nRun: `gh pr view <pr> --repo suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test --json body,headRefOid,state`; `gh pr checks <pr> --repo suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test` (or read the `test` workflow run for the head SHA); and run `npm ci && npm test` at the repo root at the head. Also check that no other open PR on the repo claims issue 102 for this change (`gh pr list --repo suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test --search 102`).\nPASS: the PR is on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test, its body contains `Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102`, the `test` workflow at the head commit completed successfully, the local `npm test` passes, and the change is in that single PR.\nFAIL: the body lacks that text, the test workflow at the head is failing, missing or still pending, local `npm test` fails, or the change is split across more than one PR.\n\nAdvisory (not pass/fail conditions):\n- Check that `package-lock.json` includes the new workspace; without it `npm ci` fails in CI.\n- The CLI ideally prints errors to stdout and exits 0/1 without stray stderr output in the normal path; a trailing newline at the end of a file should not produce a reported empty row; CRLF line endings ideally do not cause false errors.\n- The bin file ideally has a `#!/usr/bin/env node` shebang and a `bin` entry in package.json."}